  "live_records": {
    "q-68390": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68390",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Andry is planning a party. He made $30$ sandwiches for $12$ people at the last party. If there is a proportional relationship between the number of people at the party $x$ and the number of sandwiches $y,$ what is the constant of proportionality for the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that Andry made $y=30$ sandwiches for $x=12$ people.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{30}{12}=\\frac{30÷6}{12÷6}=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $\\frac{5}{2},$ and its units are \"sandwiches per person.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
