    "q-91985": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91985",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Tom purchased $7$ gallons of gas for $$21$ dollars. If there is a proportional relationship between the cost of gas $y$ (in dollars) and the volume of gas $x$ (in gallons), what is the constant of proportionality for the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that Tom paid $y=21$ dollars for $x=7$ gallons of gas.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{21}{7}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $3$, and its units are \"dollars per gallon.\"",
