    "q-68403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68403",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Caroline bought a new car. The company claims she can drive the vehicle for $120$ miles with $4$ gallons of gasoline. If there is a proportional relationship between the volume of gas $x$ (in gallons) and the distance traveled $y$ (in miles), what is the constant of proportionality for the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that Caroline can drive the car for $y=120$ miles with $x=4$ gallons of gasoline.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{120}{4}=\\frac{120÷4}{4÷4}=\\frac{30}{1}=30\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $30$, and its units are \"miles per gallon.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
