    "q-115573": {
      "dom_id": "step-q115573",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "In a direct variation, $f=84$ when $g=-7.$ What is the relationship between $f$ and $g?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f$ varies directly with $g,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\nf=kg.\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that $f=84$ when $g=-7$ to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84 & =k\\cdot (-7) \\\\ \\frac{84}{(-7)} & =k \\\\ -\\frac{84}{7} & =k \\\\ -12 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our direct variation equation is\n\n$$\nf=-12g.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
